## WHEN IN DOUBT

1. **Check existing similar code** - Look at how it's done elsewhere
2. **Read lib/supabase.ts** - Understand the types
3. **Check database schema** - Verify column names and types
4. **Test incrementally** - Don't change too much at once
5. **Ask for clarification** - Better to ask than assume

## REMEMBER

- **Always update related files together** (use file relationship maps above)
- **Keep types in sync with database** (lib/supabase.ts is critical)
- **Test on mobile** (50% of users are mobile)
- **Email notifications matter** (users expect confirmation)
- **Credits are the core** (all transactions must be logged)
- **RLS is security** (never skip row level security)
- **Admins are special** (check admin_users table)

## QUICK REFERENCE

**Most frequently edited files:**
1. lib/supabase.ts - Types (edit when database changes)
2. app/dashboard/page.tsx - Main user interface
3. app/profile/page.tsx - User profile editing
4. app/admin/events/page.tsx - Admin event management
5. lib/email.ts - Email notifications

**Most common tasks:**
1. Adding database field → Update 3+ files (schema, types, displays)
2. Adding new page → Create page.tsx, add navigation link
3. Email notification → Add function to lib/email.ts, call from action
4. Admin feature → Create in app/admin/, check admin_users table
5. API endpoint → Create in app/api/, use service role

